{title: I Surrender All}
{lyricist: Judson W. Van DeVenter}
{composer: Winfield S. Weeden}
{year: 1896}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune SURRENDER}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to SURRENDER}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags commitment, invitation}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]All to Jesus [G]I sur[D]render,
[D]All to Him I [E7]freely [A]give;
[D]I will ever [G]love and [D]trust Him,
[D]In His [A]presence [A7]daily [D]live.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]I sur[G]render [D]all,
[D]I sur[E7]render [A]all;
[D]All to [D7]Thee, my [G]blessed [D]Savior,
[D]I sur[A7]render [D]all.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]All to Jesus [G]I sur[D]render,
[D]Humbly at His [E7]feet I [A]bow,
[D]Worldly pleasures [G]all for[D]saken;
[D]Take me, [A]Jesus, [A7]take me [D]now.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]All to Jesus [G]I sur[D]render;
[D]Make me, Savior, [E7]wholly [A]Thine;
[D]Let me feel the [G]Holy [D]Spirit,
[D]Truly [A]know that [A7]Thou art [D]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]All to Jesus [G]I sur[D]render;
[D]Lord, I give my[E7]self to [A]Thee;
[D]Fill me with Thy [G]love and [D]power;
[D]Let Thy [A]blessing [A7]fall on [D]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]All to Jesus [G]I sur[D]render;
[D]Now I feel the [E7]sacred [A]flame.
[D]O the joy of [G]full sal[D]vation!
[D]Glory, [A]glory, [A7]to His [D]name!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
